<meta name="description" content="After disaster strikes, people’s lives can be turned upside down. It can be difficult to recover and rebuild. People with disabilities may face additional hardships trying to get help after disasters. By law, the federal government must incorporate the needs of people with disabilities into disaster planning and response. But is it doing enough?" />
